<!-- The hub plus one URL per game. These used to be ?game= query URLs over a
     single shared document — self-canonicalising, so at least not competing with
     each other, but still eleven addresses serving byte-identical HTML that only
     JavaScript told apart. They are now real directories, each a file of its own
     with its own <head>, <h1> and standing copy (build_pages.js), which is the
     first version of this list where the URLs point at genuinely different pages.

     The OLD ?game= URLs are deliberately not listed. They still work and still
     open the right game — app.js rewrites the address to the new path on arrival,
     which folds the old URL into the new one instead of keeping two live
     addresses for one game.

     Records and Archive are left out, as before: they show nothing but the
     visitor's own saved scores. Mode URLs (?mode=practice) are left out too —
     all ~32 serve the same document, so a mode is a state of a page, not a page.

     The EuroCup has its own hub and its own page for each of the seven games it
     plays (/eurocup/…, also build_pages.js), with EuroCup copy — they are about
     different players, not duplicates of the EuroLeague pages. -->
